# Deployment

Deployment means putting the app online so other users can access it.

Our project has two main parts:

```text
front
server
```

The frontend is Next.js.

The backend is Express.js.

## Simple Deployment Structure

```text
Frontend -> Vercel
Backend -> Railway, Render, Fly.io, or VPS
Database -> MongoDB Atlas, Postgres, or another hosted database
Vector DB -> Pinecone, Qdrant, Chroma, MongoDB Atlas Vector Search, or pgvector
```

## Environment Variables

Production needs environment variables.

Examples:

```env
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=5000
CLIENT_URL=https://your-frontend.com
CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend.com
LLM_PROVIDER=github
GITHUB_TOKEN=your_secret_token
```

Secrets should not be written in code.

They should live in the hosting platform environment settings.

## Frontend Deployment

The frontend needs to know the backend URL.

Example:

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-backend.com/api
```

## Backend Deployment

The backend needs:

```text
model API keys
database URL
vector database URL
CORS origins
upload limits
```

## Deployment Checklist

```text
Frontend builds successfully
Backend starts successfully
Environment variables are set
CORS allows the frontend domain
Uploads work
Indexing works
Chat works
Logs are visible
Secrets are not exposed
```

